# npm release on master

Any user-facing or publishable change that will merge to `master` **must** include a Changeset in the same PR (or a follow-up PR before expecting npm to update).

## Required workflow

1. Add `.changeset/*.md` via `pnpm changeset` (or an equivalent markdown file).
2. Bump all three fixed packages together: `@drawink/core`, `@drawink/vue`, `@drawink/react`.
3. Prefer `minor` for new capabilities, `patch` for fixes/docs-only publishable tweaks, `major` only for breaking API changes.
4. After the feature/fix merges to `master`, the Release workflow opens a **Version Packages** PR — merge that PR so `pnpm release` publishes to npm.
5. Do **not** tell the user npm will update until a changeset exists (or the Version Packages PR is ready to merge).

## Do not

- Merge publishable work to `master` without a changeset and then say “just wait for npm”.
- Publish only one of the three `@drawink/*` packages in isolation.
